# a small body (an asteroid, a comet's nucleus, a Kuiper body): a world like any, made by the same ground system, with its radius from
# the body and its grains from the body's own mix; its relief a share of its radius (lumps and craters), no air, no seas, no life
@terrain asteroid
albedo: 0.15
name: A small body
radius-km: 10
solid: yes
water: no
clouds: no
air-km: 0
rock-colour: 0.46 0.43 0.4
base-k: 180
relief-of-radius: 0.18
land-share: 1
polar-ice: no
life: no
rivers: no
volcano-count: 0
day-hours: 6..30
# (grains below: the ground's make-up only until the body's own mix replaces it; every rock has one of its own, so in practice it is never read)
grains: asteroid-s

